            {
              "$type": "Models.Factorial.Experiment, Models",
              "DisabledSimNames": null,
              "Name": "SFFFCultivarTrial_Waikato",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                  "Text": "### Plantain Potency and Practice SFFF, Waikato site\r\n\r\nSimulation setup based on plantain small plot field trials conducted at DairyNZ site in Waikato (-37.769011, 175.369699), New Zealand, during 2022-2024. The experiment consisted of a randomised complete block design with 20 cultivar treatments and five blocks. The treatments consisted of nine breeding lines and nine commercially available diploid plantain cultivars and two diploid ryegrass control (cv. “Legion AR37”). Legion AR37 is marketed as a perennial ryegrass, however, it is certified as Lolium x boucheanum Kunth due to a small number of tip awns. To maintain experimental integrity, the identities of the plantain cultivars were blinded by assigning each a number from one to twenty. In this simulation all plantain cultivars are included, but only the cultivars for which APSIM is parameterised for are enabled.  \n\nThe soil at the experimental site was a Typic Sandy Gley. Soil tests to 75 mm depth were conducted at the experimental site and showed pH of 5.9, Olsen P (mg L-1) of 36, K (me100g-1) of 0.67, Ca (me 100g-1) of 7.9, Mg (me 100g-1) of 1.3, Na (me 100g-1) of 0.11, Cation Exchange Capacity (me 100g-1) of 20, Sulphate S (mg kg-1) of 25, and Organic S (mg kg-1) of 12. This site was grazed pasture previously, it received a double spray with a glyphosate product four weeks apart, then ploughed, power-harrowed, rolled, and levelled to create a firm, fine seedbed.  \n\nWeather data was obtained from nearby weather station (NIWA).  \n",
                  "Name": "Memo",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                },
