            {
              "$type": "Models.Factorial.Experiment, Models",
              "DisabledSimNames": null,
              "Name": "SFFFCultivarTrial_Manawatu",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                  "Text": "### Plantain Potency and Practice SFFF, Manawatu site\n\nSimulation setup based on plantain small plot field trials conducted at the Agricom site in Manawatū (-40.121756, 175.642837), New Zealand, during 2022-2024. The experiment consisted of a randomised complete block design with 10 cultivar treatments and five blocks. The treatments consisted of nine commercially available diploid plantain cultivars and a diploid ryegrass control (cv. “Legion AR37”). Legion AR37 is marketed as a perennial ryegrass, however, it is certified as Lolium x boucheanum Kunth due to a small number of tip awns. To maintain experimental integrity, the identities of the plantain cultivars were blinded by assigning each a number from one to nine. In this simulation all plantain cultivars are included, but only the cultivars for which APSIM is parameterised for are enabled.  \n\nThe soil at the experimental site was Argillic-fragic Perch-gley Pallic. Soil tests to 75 mm depth were conducted at the experimental site and showed pH of 5.9, Olsen P (mg L-1) of 22, K (me100g-1) of 0.17, Ca (me 100g-1) of 7.7, Mg (me 100g-1) of 0.78, Na (me 100g-1) of 0.10, Cation Exchange Capacity (me 100g-1) of 15, Sulphate S (mg kg-1) of 6, Organic S (mg kg-1) of 6, potentially available N (kg ha-1) of 183 and anaerobically mineralisable N (ug kg-1) of 141. This site was non-grazed maize crop previously, it was ploughed, power-harrowed, rolled, and levelled to create a firm, fine seedbed.  \n\nWeather data was obtained from nearby weather station (NIWA).  \r\n\r\n",
                  "Name": "Memo",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                },
