              ],
              "Name": "LincolnMix",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                  "Text": "### Lincoln Univerity, Thinzar Soe Myint PhD\r\n\r\nSimulation setup was based on a pasture mixture with plantain experiment conducted at Lincoln University (-43.3857, 172.2800), New Zealand, between 2017 and 2021. The original experiment included ten mixtures of perennial ryegrass (cv. Rely AR37), white clover (cv. Quartz), and plantain (cv. Tonic) which were grown with and without N fertiliser under irrigated condition (Soe Myint et al., 2022). The mixtures, in brief, comprised three single-species mixtures (monocultures), three binary mixtures (50% of each of two species), one three-species mixture (33.3% of each species), and three mixtures dominated in turn by each species (66.6% of one species and 16.6% of each of the other two species). This simulation only includes the plantain monoculture with and without N fertiliser at two seed densities (1000 and 2000 seeds/m2). The annual irrigation was 220 mm in the 2017/2018 season, 217 mm in the 2018/2019 season, 435 mm in the 2019/2020 season, and 540 mm in the 2020/2021 growing season.  \n\nThe soil type is a Wakanui silt loam and classified as a Mottled Immature Pallic Soil in the New Zealand Soil Classification and Udic Ustochrept in USDA Soil Taxonomy. The soil had a medium fertility (pH 6, Olsen P 16 mg/L, Ca 7.3 me/100 g, Mg 0.98 me/100 g, K 0.40 me/100 g, Na 0.14 me/100 g and SO4-S 4 μg/g in top 75 mm) when sampled on 20 March 2017. This site was grazed pasture previously and was sprayed out on 16 March 2017 (glyphosate, 470 g/L at 2 L/ha with 200 L/ha water; WeedMaster TS470, Nufarm, NZ), cultivated on 22 March 2017 (rota crumbler), fertilised on 23 March 2017 (9% P, 11% S, 20% Ca at 300 kg/ha; Superphosphate, Ravensdown, NZ), cultivated into a seed bed on 29 March 2017 (heavy grubber then power harrow and Cambridge roller).  \n\nWeather data was obtained from nearby weather station (NIWA).  \n",
                  "Name": "Memo",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                },
